>But then the state of grammar
>education in America really sucks.

Amen!
Most often, the teachers themselves don't even know what it is they are
trying to teach.
I have read grammar books that contradicted themselves, but most often, the
best ones remember that English grammar is "not set in stone", so they cover
their mistakes by saying that it can be interpreted either way.

I've been taught both that "is" is a linking (or helping, or auxilliary, and
so on...) verb, but I've also been taught that "is" is the main verb, even
in the case of "Is going" or "is becoming", when "going" or "becoming" are
participles, interpreted as either adjectives or nouns or...

Blech.

Nate

